  "Id": 3099,
  "Title": "Addition of mental health to the lady health worker curriculum in Pakistan: now or never",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Bridging the mental healthcare gap in Pakistan",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Lady Health workers (LHWs) are a critical component of Pakistan's primary healthcare system, providing care to underserved and remote communities. However, their training does not include mental health, leaving them ill-equipped to identify and address mental health issues in their patients. This has resulted in a significant treatment gap, with the majority of people with mental health problems in Pakistan remaining untreated."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "article",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "link",
                "attrs": {
                  "href": "https://human-resources-health.biomedcentral.com/articles/10.1186/s12960-023-00814-8",
                  "target": "_self",
                  "linktype": "url",
                  "uuid": null,
                  "anchor": null,
                  "custom": {}
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " \"Addition of mental health to the lady health worker curriculum in Pakistan: now or never\" highlights the urgent need to incorporate mental health education into the training curriculum of Lady Health Workers (LHWs) in Pakistan. The authors argue that mental health issues have long been neglected in the country's healthcare system, despite their prevalence and impact on individuals and communities."
          },
          {
            "type": "hard_break"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The authors suggest that the inclusion of mental health education in the LHW curriculum could help bridge this gap. They argue that LHWs have a unique advantage in addressing mental health issues, as they are trusted members of their communities and can provide culturally sensitive care."
          },
          {
            "type": "hard_break"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Furthermore, the authors emphasize that mental health issues are not limited to urban areas but are prevalent in rural communities as well. Therefore, it is crucial to train LHWs in mental health to ensure that mental health services reach all communities, regardless of their location."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The authors also recognize that incorporating mental health into the LHW curriculum is not without its challenges. For example, it would require significant changes to the existing curriculum and training programs. However, they argue that the benefits of doing so far outweigh the challenges and that failure to act now would perpetuate the neglect of mental health in Pakistan's healthcare system."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In conclusion, the article highlights the urgent need to include mental health education in the LHW curriculum in Pakistan. Doing so would help bridge the treatment gap for mental health issues and ensure that mental "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "health services reach all communities in the country. It is a crucial step towards improving the overall health and well-being of the population."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Read full article ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "italic"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "here",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "italic"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "attrs": {
                  "href": "https://human-resources-health.biomedcentral.com/articles/10.1186/s12960-023-00814-8",
                  "target": "_self",
                  "linktype": "url",
                  "uuid": null,
                  "anchor": null,
                  "custom": {}
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " as published in Human Resource Health. ",
            "marks": [
              {
